CIPrimes -- compute the symbolic power by taking the intersection of the powers of the primary components
*********************************************************************************************************

Description
===========

The default value is false.  When defined to be true, the *note symbolicPower:
symbolicPower, function tests whether the primary components are complete
intersections having the same height.  If each component is, then the function
takes the intersection of the powers of the components: $$I^{(n)}=\cap_{p\in
Ass(R/I)} p^n.$$

See also
========

  * *note containmentProblem: containmentProblem, -- computes the smallest
    symbolic power contained in a power of an ideal.
  * *note isSymbPowerContainedinPower: isSymbPowerContainedinPower, -- tests if
    the m-th symbolic power an ideal is contained the n-th power
  * *note symbolicDefect: symbolicDefect, -- computes the symbolic defect of an
    ideal
  * *note symbolicPower: symbolicPower, -- computes the symbolic power of an
    ideal.

