containmentProblem -- computes the smallest symbolic power contained in a power of an ideal.
********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        containmentProblem(I,n)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note CIPrimes: CIPrimes, => ..., default value false, compute the
        symbolic power by taking the intersection of the powers of the primary
        components
      * *note InSymbolic: containmentProblem_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmInSymbolic=>_pd_pd_
        pd_rp, => ..., default value false, an optional parameter used in
        containmentProblem.
      * *note UseMinimalPrimes: UseMinimalPrimes, => ..., default value false,
        an option to only use minimal primes to calculate symbolic powers
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the minimum value m such that the
        m-th symbolic power of I is contained in I^n

Description
===========

Given an ideal $I$ and an integer $n$, containementProblem returns the order of
the smallest symbolic power of $I$ contained in $I^n$.



+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : B = QQ[x,y,z];                |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : f = map(QQ[t],B,{t^3,t^4,t^5})|
