        $I^n==I^{(n)}$

Description
===========

Given a radical ideal I and an integer $n$, this method returns true if and
only if $I^n=I^{(n)}$. This method circumvents computing the symbolic powers in
most cases, by first testing the *note bigHeight: bigHeight, of $I^n$



+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : B = QQ[x,y,z];                |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : f = map(QQ[t],B,{t^3,t^4,t^5})|
|                                   |
|                      3   4   5    |
|o2 = map (QQ[t], B, {t , t , t })  |
|                                   |
|o2 : RingMap QQ[t] <-- B           |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ker f;                    |
|                                   |
|o3 : Ideal of B                    |
+-----------------------------------+
|i4 : isSymbolicEqualOrdinary(I,2)  |
|                                   |
|o4 = false                         |
+-----------------------------------+

