lowerBoundResurgence -- computes a lower bound for the resurgence of a given ideal.
***********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        lowerBoundResurgence(Ideal)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note SampleSize: lowerBoundResurgence_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmSampleSize=>_pd_pd
        _pd_rp, => ..., default value 5, optional parameter used for
        approximating asymptotic invariants that are defined as limits.
      * *note UseWaldschmidt: lowerBoundResurgence_lp_pd_pd_pd_cmUseWaldschmidt
        =>_pd_pd_pd_rp, => ..., default value false, optional input for
        computing a lower bound for the resurgence of a given ideal.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, 

Description
===========

The resurgence of an ideal $I$, defined by Harbourne and Bocci, is given by
$\rho(I) :=$ sup $\lbrace a/b : I^{(a)}$ &nsub; $I^b \rbrace.$

Given an ideal $I$, finds the maximum of the quotients $m/k$ that fail $I^{(m)}
\subseteq I^k$ with $k \leq$ the optional input SampleSize.



+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = QQ[x,y,z];                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = intersect(ideal"x,y",ideal"x,z",ideal"y,z");|
|                                                     |
|o2 : Ideal of T                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : lowerBoundResurgence(I)                         |
|                                                     |
|     6                                               |
|o3 = -                                               |
|     5                                               |
|                                                     |
|o3 : QQ                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

