File: SymbolicPowers.info, Node: symbPowerPrimePosChar, Next: The Containment Problem, Prev: symbolicPowerJoin, Up: Top

symbPowerPrimePosChar
*********************

  * Usage: 
        symbPowerPrimePosChar(I,n)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the n-th symbolic power of I

Description
===========

Given a prime ideal $I$ in a polynomial ring over a field of positive
characteristic, and an integer $n$, this method returns the $n$-th symbolic
power of $I$.  To compute $I^{(a)}$, find the largest value $k$ with $q = p^k
\leq a$. Then $I^{(a)} = (I^{[q]} : I^{a-q+1})$.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : B = ZZ/7[x,y,z];                                                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : f = map(ZZ/7[t],B,{t^3,t^4,t^5})                                        |
|                                                                             |
|          ZZ          3   4   5                                              |
|o2 = map (--[t], B, {t , t , t })                                            |
|           7                                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|             ZZ                                                              |
|o2 : RingMap --[t] <-- B                                                     |
|              7                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ker f;                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of B                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : symbPowerPrimePosChar(I,2)                                              |
|                                                                             |
|             4       2     2 2   2 3    3       2 2      3   3 2    4     3  |
|o4 = ideal (y  - 2x*y z + x z , x y  - x y*z - y z  + x*z , x y  - x z - y z |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|            2   5      3     2       3                                       |
|     + x*y*z , x  + x*y  - 3x y*z + z )                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of B                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The ideal must be prime.

See also
========

  * *note symbolicPower: symbolicPower, -- computes the symbolic power of an
    ideal.

