UseWaldschmidt -- optional input for computing a lower bound for the resurgence of a given ideal.
*************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        lowerBoundResurgence(Ideal,UseWaldschmidt=>true)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, 

Description
===========

Given an ideal $I$ and an integer $n$, returns the larger value between the
maximum of the quotients $m/k$ that fail $I^{(m)} \subseteq I^k$ with $k \leq
n$ and $\frac{\alpha(I)}{waldschmidt(I)}$.



+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = QQ[x,y,z];                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = intersect(ideal"x,y",ideal"x,z",ideal"y,z");|
|                                                     |
|o2 : Ideal of T                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : lowerBoundResurgence(I,UseWaldschmidt=>true)    |
|                                                     |
|     4                                               |
|o3 = -                                               |
|     3                                               |
|                                                     |
|o3 : QQ                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------+

